{"w": 595.3200073242188, "h": 809.0257568359375, "lines": [{"t": "96", "x": 0.9036148555787364, "y": 0.9742087522985531, "w": 0.03012839302489931, "h": 0.017428414981790374, "c": 1, "size": 12.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "READING PASSAGE 3", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.16787843496658414, "w": 0.29152886031313374, "h": 0.023179739115831682, "c": 1, "size": 16.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "You should spend about 20 minutes on Question 27 – 40, which are based on", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.21255440745048804, "w": 0.8270932289137184, "h": 0.02039118517446672, "c": 1, "size": 14.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "Reading Passage 3 below", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.2431096406977009, "w": 0.277090834956047, "h": 0.02039118517446672, "c": 1, "size": 14.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Robots and us", "x": 0.416129128333868, "y": 0.2835879577623006, "w": 0.21065645907721595, "h": 0.026142565890596797, "c": 1, "size": 18.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "Three leaders in their fields answer questions about our relationships with robot", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.33266926079197723, "w": 0.8157718083648674, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "When asked 'Should robots be used to colonies other planets?', cosmology and", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.37093746260866967, "w": 0.8265333401409902, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "astrophysics Professor Martin Rees said he believed the solar system would be", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.39911952988884714, "w": 0.8259032217749058, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "mapped by robotic craft by the end of the century. 'The next step would be mining", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.4274498799629847, "w": 0.8263817057343129, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "of asteroids, enabling fabrication of large structures in space without having to", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.4557802677585149, "w": 0.8263778097860683, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "bring all the raw materials from Earth. ... I think this is more realistic and benign", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.48413536306613963, "w": 0.8265290340929304, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "than the … \"terraforming\"* of planets.' He maintains that colonised planets", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.5124657131402772, "w": 0.8266633417824147, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "'should be preserved with a status that is analogous to Antarctica here on Earth.'", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.5407961009358074, "w": 0.8230284220702188, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "On the question of using robots to colonise other planets and exploit mineral", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.5790643404738923, "w": 0.8257940326991037, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "resources, engineering Professor Daniel Wolpert replied, 'I don't see a pressing", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.6073947282694225, "w": 0.8259900604107785, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "need to colonise other planets unless we can bring [these] resources back to", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.6357251160649526, "w": 0.8267118360855644, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Earth. The vast majority of Earth is currently inaccessible to us. Using robots to", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.6640925085465359, "w": 0.8260553688063522, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "gather resources nearer to home would seem to be a better use of our robotic", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.6924229340634586, "w": 0.8259250595900662, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "tools.'", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.7206049636222435, "w": 0.06656130177164145, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Meanwhile, for anthropology Professor Kathleen Richardson, the idea of", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.7588732408817209, "w": 0.8260988393867654, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "'colonisation' of other planets seemed morally dubious: 'I think whether we do", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.7872035909558586, "w": 0.826131134747214, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "something on Earth or on Mars we should always do it in the spirit of a genuine", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.8155339410299962, "w": 0.8258594436196312, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "interest in \"the Other\", not to impose a particular model, but to meet \"the Other\".'", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.8438643665469189, "w": 0.8268583442445515, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "In response to the second question, 'How soon will machine intelligence outstrip", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.8821573135970984, "w": 0.8262319167768041, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "human intelligence?', Rees mentions robots that are advanced enough to beat", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.9103393431558834, "w": 0.8265447204108626, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "humans at chess, but then goes on to say, 'Robots are still limited in their ability", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.938669693230021, "w": 0.8259900604107785, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}], "source": "pdf text layer"}